ecially if your plans\nincluding recreating or commuting across eastern Utah and western\nColorado Sunday onward. Also, keep in mind weather potential above\nyour location and upstream, particularly for those who reside below\nsensitive terrain like recent burn scars.","ends":"2026-10-12T18:00:00-06:00","severity":"Unknown","areaDesc":"Archuleta, CO; Delta, CO; Dolores, CO; Garfield, CO; Hinsdale, CO; La Plata, CO; Mesa, CO; Moffat, CO; Montezuma, CO; Montrose, CO; Ouray, CO; Rio Blanco, CO; San Juan, CO; San Miguel, CO; Daggett, UT; Grand, UT; San Juan, UT; Uintah, UT","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.5953c0ab1d0bcab0b29fc3e9364e3d17cf28daf6.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-12T11:54:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KGJT 121154 AFDGJT Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Grand Junction CO 554 AM MDT Mon Oct 12 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - An additional 1-2\" of precipitation is expected over the high terrain through Wednesday, with locally higher amounts likely over the Uintas. Some of this will be in the form of snow down to 9000 feet...but most significant above 10000 feet. - Winds will be","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=AFD&format=CI"},"hwo":null,"fwf":{"office":"GJT","issued":"2026-10-12T09:00:00+00:00","snippet":".DISCUSSION... Showers and thunderstorms will continue today. A few storms could produce heavy rainfall rates, leading to flash flooding risk in eastern UT and western CO. Winds remain strong today with gusts up to 40 mph. Critical fire weather conditions do not develop this week, as relative humidity remains elevated and winds become lighter. Showers and thunderstorms will continue through Wednes","url":"https://forecast.weather.gov/product.php?site=GJT&issuedby=GJT&product=FWF&format=CI"},"coagmet":{"station_id":"dlr01","station_name":"Dolores","distance_km":9.1,"soil_temp_5cm_f